                <pb facs="0153" n="69" sameAs="frus:frus1903/pg69"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Prince Ch’ing to Mr.
                            Conger.</hi></head>
                <p>Concerning the matter of opening ports in the three eastern provinces
                    (Manchuria), which I, the Prince, yesterday discussed in a personal interview
                    with your excellency, China has already had the intention to open and establish
                    commercial ports at two of the places which we mentioned, but it will be
                    necessary to wait until the Russian troops now temporarily occupying the Three
                    Eastern Provinces shall be entirely withdrawn and the local government handed
                    back, when China herself will open them.</p>
                <closer><dateline rendition="#float-left"><date
                            calendar="chinese-lunisolar gregorian" when="1903-07-20">Intercalary
                            Fifth Moon, 26th day (July 20, 1903)</date>.</dateline></closer>
            </div>
